{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-classical-limit-obstruction","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:classical-limit-obstruction","kind":"definition","title":"The classical limit obstruction of a quantum universe","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hochschild-homology","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-classical-limit-functor","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-characteristic-classes"],"cites":["references/yekutieli2010"],"tags":["obstruction","classical-limit","hochschild-cohomology","deformation-theory","q-to-1"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction","text":"classical-limit-obstruction.md","leanSource":"classical-limit-obstruction.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:classical-limit-obstruction\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum universe over a Noetherian ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> with substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> and classical limit functor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L} : \\mathbf{C}_q \\to \\mathbf{C}_1</code> (<a href=\"#def:classical-limit-functor\" data-at=\"stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-construction\">classical limit functor</a>). The <strong>classical limit obstruction</strong> of the quantum universe is the Hochschild cohomology group</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">\\mathrm{Obs}(\\mathbf{C}, q \\to 1)\n := \nHH^2(\\mathcal{U}_q(\\mathfrak{g}), \\mathrm{Ad})</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{U}_q(\\mathfrak{g})</code> is the Lusztig integral form of the quantized enveloping algebra associated to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Ad}</code> denotes the adjoint bimodule.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-obstruction.md","heading":"Definition","number":"21.4.5","page":"b/def-classical-limit-obstruction","qa":{"counts":{"pass":85,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":16,"unknown":0,"stale":76},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Core.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-obstruction.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
